  "origin": "Public-domain books and cultural-heritage texts aggregated from Project Gutenberg and Wikisource, with spelling and OCR errors corrected by Pleias using its own OCR-correction models (PleIAs/OCRonos and the PleIAs/Post-OCR-Correction dataset pipeline). Harmful/toxic content removed via the Celadon toxicity classifier, and low-educational-value content filtered out. OpenCulture is the largest Common Corpus collection at ~967B tokens. Form: public-domain text + machine OCR-corrected + toxicity-filtered. Note: the license field uses the CC Public Domain Mark IRI per the interim convention; the underlying works are public domain by copyright expiration, a jurisdiction-dependent status (a work PD in one country may still be in copyright in another). The `licenseScope` field (added to 0.0.1 after this stress test surfaced Gap A) carries a copyright-expiration jurisdiction clause to qualify the PD claim — see notes/stress-test-pleias-common-corpus.md (Gap A). The OCR-correction and toxicity-filtering steps are transformative custody hops performed by an LLM-based pipeline.",
